Here's a JavaScript implementation for packing and unpacking an array of entities into an ArrayBuffer. The entities have the fields `id` (4 bits) and `size` (3 bits).

```javascript
function packEntities(entities) {
  const buffer = new ArrayBuffer(entities.length);
  const view = new DataView(buffer);

  for (let i = 0; i < entities.length; i++) {
    const entity = entities[i];
    const id = entity.id & 0xF; // Masking to get the 4 least significant bits
    const size = entity.size & 0x7; // Masking to get the 3 least significant bits

    // Write the id and size to the buffer
    view.setUint16(i * (id + size), id | (size << 3), true);

    // Write the entity data, assuming it's a Uint8Array
    if (entity.data) {
      const dataLength = entity.data.length;
      if (dataLength > 255) {
        throw new Error("Entity data size exceeds the maximum allowed size.");
      }
      view.setUint8(i * (id + size) + 2, dataLength);
      view.setUint8Array(i * (id + size) + 3, entity.data, 0, dataLength);
    }
  }

  return buffer;
}

function unpackEntities(buffer, count) {
  const view = new DataView(buffer);
  const entities = [];

  for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {
    const id = view.getUint16(i) & 0x0FFF; // Masking to get the 4 least significant bits for id and the 3 least significant bits for size
    const size = id >> 3;
    const dataLength = view.getUint8(i + 1);

    // Read the entity data, assuming it's a Uint8Array
    const entityData = new Uint8Array(dataLength);
    view.getUint8Array(i + 3, entityData, 0, dataLength);

    entities.push({
      id: id & 0xF,
      size: size,
      data: entityData
    });
  }

  return entities;
}
```

In the `packEntities` function, we create an ArrayBuffer and a DataView to work with the buffer. We iterate through the entities and write their id, size, and data to the buffer. The id and size are written as 16-bit unsigned integers, with the id in the lower 4 bits and the size in the upper 3 bits. The data length is written as an 8-bit unsigned integer.

In the `unpackEntities` function, we create a DataView to work with the buffer and an empty array to store the unpacked entities. We iterate through the buffer and read the id, size, and data for each entity. The id and size are read as 16-bit unsigned integers, with the id in the lower 4 bits and the size in the upper 3 bits. The data length is read as an 8-bit unsigned integer. We then create a new Uint8Array for the entity data and read it from the buffer. Finally, we push the unpacked entity into the entities array.

